# Flight Booking & Payment Routing Implementation

This document provides a comprehensive overview of the implementation, architecture, and step-by-step test cases for the custom booking payment routing system on **ezeeFlights**.

---

## 1. Overview & Architecture

To support diverse checkout strategies, the flight booking flow dynamically routes inquiries and payment gateways based on user selections:

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[Start Booking Page] --> B{Is Bid Deal?}
    B -- Yes --> C[Status: pending_payment] --> D[Create Bid Deposit Order] --> E[Launch Razorpay Deposit Widget]
    B -- No --> F{Refund Shield OR Affirm Selected?}
    F -- Yes --> G[Status: pending_payment] --> H[Backend /payments/initiate Razorpay] --> I[Launch Razorpay Advanced Widget]
    F -- No --> J[Status: confirmed] --> K[Submit Inquiry & Skip Gateway] --> L[Booking Success Screen]
```

### The Four Payment Flows

1. **Standby Bid Flow (`isBid`):** Used when the user places a bid on a standby flight deal. A fully refundable deposit is processed immediately using Razorpay to lock in the standby price.
2. **Refund Shield Flow:** When selected, a **10% discount** is applied to the booking subtotal (including seats, ancillaries, and addons). The booking is submitted as `pending_payment` and checked out via Razorpay.
3. **Affirm Flow:** To unify the user experience and support global regions, the legacy Affirm SDK is bypassed. Instead, Affirm installment bookings are routed to Razorpay (which supports native EMI/installment payment options).
4. **Standard Booking Flow:** When no bid, refund shield, or Affirm is selected, the flight is booked immediately without upfront payment. The inquiry is submitted as `confirmed` and manual/offline payment is arranged later.

